# Orca'H&M server: one profile per target, with only what the server needs to start. Everything else
# (Jellyfin, the library folder, TMDB, the sites, downloads) is set from the panel and kept in the
# database: open the panel after starting the server and it walks you through it.
#
# `pnpm setup:hm` (from the repo root) asks for these and writes profiles/<name>.env for you. By hand:
# copy this file to profiles/<name>.env (never committed) and run HM_PROFILE=<name> pnpm dev:hm.
# Nothing has a default: every value below is only a suggestion. Give every profile its own DB_FILE:
# what it records points at that target's library.

# --- required
# DB_FILE=./data/<name>.sqlite
# HOST=127.0.0.1
# PORT=8787

# --- optional
# Absolute path of the built panel, once there is one.
# WEB_ROOT=
# Set to true only behind HTTPS.
# SECURE_COOKIES=false
# Overrides the device id generated once and kept in the database.
# DEVICE_ID=
